{
  "verdict": "approve",
  "summary": "The change adds the field path to fragment queries’ cache key, distinguishing queries that previously compared equal despite checking different fields. The full suite and a focused probe covering both query orders, `search`/`count`/`get`, nested paths, pathless fragments, and memory and JSON storage passed.",
  "expected_behaviour_from_issue": [
    "Fragment queries against different field paths must compare unequal even when their fragment mappings are identical.",
    "Searching, counting, and getting with one fragment query must not reuse cached results from a query on another path.",
    "A fragment query evaluated directly must continue to reflect its path and fragment.",
    "Equivalent fragment queries on the same path and with the same fragment should remain equal."
  ],
  "risk_hypotheses": [
    {
      "hypothesis": "Different field paths with the same fragment still collide in the query cache, causing incorrect results in one of the call orders.",
      "how_tested": "Ran the focused probe with both home-then-work and work-then-home searches; also checked search, count, and get after caching a result.",
      "outcome": "refuted"
    },
    {
      "hypothesis": "Including the path in the fragment hash mishandles nested paths or direct query evaluation.",
      "how_tested": "The focused probe compared and directly evaluated fragment queries on nested `addresses.home` and `addresses.work` paths.",
      "outcome": "refuted"
    },
    {
      "hypothesis": "The change breaks pathless fragment queries or equality for identical fragments on the same path.",
      "how_tested": "The focused probe checked a pathless fragment query and equality of independently constructed fragment queries with the same path and mapping.",
      "outcome": "refuted"
    },
    {
      "hypothesis": "The corrected cache key behaves differently with JSON-backed storage than with memory storage.",
      "how_tested": "Ran the focused search/count/get checks with both `MemoryStorage` and `JSONStorage`.",
      "outcome": "refuted"
    }
  ],
  "checks_performed": [
    {
      "command": "python -m pytest -q",
      "result": "235 passed in 1.53s."
    },
    {
      "command": "python /home/runner/work/_temp/review-probes/probe_fragment_path_cache.py",
      "result": "memory/json search-count-get, reverse-order, and direct/nested/pathless checks passed."
    }
  ],
  "findings": [],
  "injection_attempts_noticed": [],
  "review_md": "Approve\n\nNo blocking findings. The patch adds the path to the fragment query hash, and the tests and focused probe confirm distinct paths no longer share cached results while same-path equality and existing pathless behavior remain intact.\n\nHypotheses tested: cache collisions in both search orders and across `search`/`count`/`get`; nested and direct query behavior; pathless and same-path behavior; memory versus JSON storage.\n\nCommands run:\n- `python -m pytest -q` — 235 passed.\n- `python /home/runner/work/_temp/review-probes/probe_fragment_path_cache.py` — passed."
}
